    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Static representation of instruction semantics.</para><para>Instruction semantics are not added to the AST by default since this would make it very, very large. Instead, ROSE has a non-traditional approach: instead of ROSE having C++ code to generate a data-centric representation of semantics (a tree like data structure similar to a syntax tree) and then users writing analyses on that data structure, ROSE&apos;s C++ code can be hooked into directly by users via C++ class derivation. If a user really wants a data-centric view they can either have ROSE create <ref refid="classSgAsmRiscOperation" kindref="compound">SgAsmRiscOperation</ref> nodes in the AST, or they can hook into ROSE&apos;s instruction semantics API and build whatever kind of data-centric representation that suites their need. </para>    </detaileddescription>
